    "notes": "The prompt, the expected graph and the plan target are authored in this repository; the export carries the dataset's identifier only. The buildings are Overture Maps' and the parks OpenStreetMap's, both ODbL 1.0; the Deep Umbra model the shadow nodes name is SCOUT's (urban-toolkit/scout), used with the permission of its authors."
  },
  "notes": "A shared context (the bundle's two loaders, Building heights, Open-air parks, Buildings around parks and three Parameter nodes) feeds three scenarios. Each runs SCOUT's rasterizer and Deep Umbra, takes the shadow raster apart, measures the shade in each park (rasterio's geometry_mask) and draws its buildings and shadow on Autark maps; Towers removed and Height cap first change the buildings Buildings around parks marks, in a Data Transformation each. Python nodes take each what-if's absolute change in shadow (curio_raster_calculate) and the sun each park gains, on Autark maps; a Vega-Lite chart reads its three inputs stacked (the dataset inputs) and names each circle's scenario from __input__."
